  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-10-25 (dev 2399d5ad7c; owner-requested re-check of the 17 actionable open P2 violated INV/META items; fixtures archived under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/premise_check_10252026/). VERDICT: PARTLY FIXED; statement re-scoped to the instantiates half. 3 of 4 members closed (INV-jukok satisfied 07-15, WI-mujor and WI-ninuv done 06-17); WI-jubag is the only open member. SOURCE half FIXED: a04ea91b99 (WI-pozur) moved synthesis after the tier filter; create_boundary_nodes collects dangling srcs (ir.py:2084); _check_dangling_endpoint (spec_validator.py:2346). Repro: a tier-4-filtered gen_pb2.py's srcs come out as python:src/gen_pb2.py:0-0:file:external_symbol placeholders; 0 edges with a missing src or dst. EXTENDS half FIXED in all 9 OO languages probed (py kt rb java ts cs swift scala php) via the core chokepoint _external_base_edge (linkers/inheritance.py:327, 70d0cc067e). INSTANTIATES half STILL VIOLATED and wider than WI-jubag says: only Python types an external constructor as instantiates; Java (new File), C# (new StringBuilder), PHP (new DateTime), TS (new Thing from lib) emit NO edge (each does emit instantiates for an in-repo new Local(), so the path is reached); Kotlin, Ruby, Swift emit plain calls; Scala emits no construction edge even in-repo. Ruby's in-repo Local.new resolves to ruby:Local:0-0:initialize:external_symbol though Local is in the same file. Both filed as separate items. NOT checked: dart, groovy, c++, objc."  # 722b
